wildos-branding (0.1.63) trixie; urgency=medium

  * A USB device plugged into a locked PC is asked about once you sign
    in, not behind the lock screen.
  * The sign-in screen only offers the fingerprint when it would be
    accepted.
  * A light on the taskbar, left of the shield, whenever any app uses the
    microphone (amber) or the camera (green), sandboxed or not. Clicking it
    shows which app and since when, with Stop to cut it off, which app used
    the other one last, and a switch for each that blocks it for every app.
    Each use is noted in Settings > System > History.
  * The Updates icon is only on the taskbar while an update downloads or
    installs, as the two-arrow icon, and only turns while the work is under
    way.
  * Notifications that arrive while the screen is locked now show on the
    lock screen. With "Quiet lock screen" on, as it is to begin with, only
    the apps and how many arrived; turned off, the title and text too.
  * Panic key, in Advanced protection: with it on, Ctrl+Alt+End locks the
    screen, clears the clipboard, its history and pinned items, and cuts
    the network and Bluetooth in one press. After unlocking, a
    notification offers to turn them back on.
  * With the guest session on, Guest is one of the accounts on the
    sign-in screen. It signs in without a password and says the desktop
    is wiped at sign-out. The screen still opens on the PC's own people
    after a guest was the last to sign in.

